<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1. </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The weight zero compactly supported cohomology <math id="S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}H_{c}^{\bullet}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}H_{c}^{\bullet}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math> is naturally isomorphic to the cohomology of the genus <math id="S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> part of the standard commutative graph complex with <math id="S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> marked external vertices <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>. Similar graph complexes arise in the study of rational homology and homotopy groups of higher dimensional long links <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>. In this paper, we use commutative graph complexes with additional decorations on the external vertices, similar to those appearing in the embedding calculus <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite> to study the next nontrivial weight-graded piece of the compactly supported cohomology of <math id="S1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Throughout, all cohomology groups are taken with rational coefficients.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The weight <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> graded piece of <math id="S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gr_{k}H_{c}^{\bullet}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}):=W_{k}H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})/W_{k-1}H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>gr</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gr_{k}H_{c}^{\bullet}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}):=W_{k}H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})/W_{k-1}H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gr_{1}H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>gr</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gr_{1}H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes for all <math id="S1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>; this follows from the vanishing of <math id="S1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\overline{{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\overline{{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, via Deligne’s weight spectral sequence. The next nontrivial weight graded piece is <math id="S1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gr_{2}H_{c}^{\bullet}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>gr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gr_{2}H_{c}^{\bullet}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math>, which we study by combining graph complex techniques with the presentations and pullback formulas for <math id="S1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{2}(\overline{{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{2}(\overline{{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math> from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Our first main result expresses <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gr_{2}H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>gr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gr_{2}H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math> as the cohomology of a graph complex <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> generated by possibly disconnected simple graphs without loops or multiple edges, with features and decorations as follows. Say the <math id="S1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-valent vertices are <span id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">external</span> and all other vertices are <span id="S1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">internal</span>.</p>
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All internal vertices are at least trivalent;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each external vertex has a label from <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\dots,n,\epsilon,\omega\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\dots,n,\epsilon,\omega\}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each label <math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math> appears exactly once, and the label <math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> appears exactly twice;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The graph obtained by joining all external vertices marked <math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> is connected and has genus <math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is no connected component consisting of a single edge connecting two external vertices with markings <math id="S1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\epsilon,\omega\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\epsilon,\omega\}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S1.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\omega,\omega\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\omega,\omega\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The edges that do not contain an external vertex with marking from <math id="S1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> are called <em id="S1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">structural</em>. Each generator is equipped with a total ordering of its structural edges, and reordering the structural edges induces multiplication by the sign of the permutation. Note that some connected components may not have any internal vertices. The <em id="S1.p3.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">degree</em> of a generator for <math id="S1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of structural edges plus one.
In figures, we replace each external vertex with its label and omit the edge ordering. For example, the following is a generator of <math id="S1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{2,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{2,2}</annotation></semantics></math> in degree <math id="S1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="S1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S1.Ex2.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="83.37" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-37.81px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 154.78 83.37" width="154.78"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,83.37) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(107.34,0) translate(0,41.69)"><path d="M 23.6 0 C 23.6 2.16 21.85 3.91 19.69 3.91 C 17.52 3.91 15.77 2.16 15.77 0 C 15.77 -2.16 17.52 -3.91 19.69 -3.91 C 21.85 -3.91 23.6 -2.16 23.6 0 Z M 19.69 0"></path><path d="M -5.93 17.05 C -5.93 19.21 -7.68 20.96 -9.84 20.96 C -12 20.96 -13.76 19.21 -13.76 17.05 C -13.76 14.89 -12 13.13 -9.84 13.13 C -7.68 13.13 -5.93 14.89 -5.93 17.05 Z M -9.84 17.05"></path><path d="M -5.93 -17.05 C -5.93 -14.89 -7.68 -13.13 -9.84 -13.13 C -12 -13.13 -13.76 -14.89 -13.76 -17.05 C -13.76 -19.21 -12 -20.96 -9.84 -20.96 C -7.68 -20.96 -5.93 -19.21 -5.93 -17.05 Z M -9.84 -17.05"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 35.91 -4.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -22.49 31.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.41em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="5.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -23.99 -37.07)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="8.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -102.73 -2.98)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="8.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -62.51 -4.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 16.06 2.1 L -6.21 14.95"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 16.06 -2.1 L -6.21 -14.95"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 23.88 0 L 31.02 0"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M -9.84 12.86 L -9.84 -12.86"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M -11.94 20.68 L -15.14 26.23"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M -11.94 -20.68 L -15.14 -26.23"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M -89.23 0 L -67.4 0"></path></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The differential <math id="S1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sum of two parts
<math id="S1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Here <math id="S1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sum over all vertices and over all ways of splitting the vertex into two vertices joined by an edge, so that the new vertices are at least trivalent.</p>
<table id="S1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta_{split}\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta_{split}\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{v\text{ vertex}}\Gamma\text{ split $v$}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> vertex</mtext></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> split </mtext><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{v\text{ vertex}}\Gamma\text{ split $v$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
