<p id="S1.p11.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a connected component with one <math id="S1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-decoration and no other external vertices. The genus <math id="S1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> of the overall graph is the sum of the genera <math id="S1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. The cohomology of the summands with <math id="S1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math> are explicitly understood, and the complementary part <math id="S1.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> contributes a tensor factor that is identified with <math id="S1.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g_{1},1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g_{1},1})</annotation></semantics></math>. In this way, one arrives at the following:</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.7</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> one has an injection</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{c}^{n-3}({\mathcal{M}}_{0,n})\otimes W_{0}H_{c}^{\bullet-n}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,1})\ \oplus\ \mathbb{B}_{n}\otimes W_{0}H_{c}^{\bullet-n-3}({\mathcal{M}}_{g-1,1})\to\gr_{2}H_{c}^{\bullet}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">⊕</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>gr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{c}^{n-3}({\mathcal{M}}_{0,n})\otimes W_{0}H_{c}^{\bullet-n}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,1})\ \oplus\ \mathbb{B}_{n}\otimes W_{0}H_{c}^{\bullet-n-3}({\mathcal{M}}_{g-1,1})\to\gr_{2}H_{c}^{\bullet}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where
<math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector space defined in (<a href="#S8.E46" title="In 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>) below, which has dimension at least <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-2)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-2)!</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
