<p id="S3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">On the right-hand side, the second sum is taken over all ways of distributing the half-edges incident to the special vertex over the two new vertices of genus <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> such that the resulting graph is stable.
Similarly, we may depict the contribution to <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{loop}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{loop}</annotation></semantics></math> from a non-special vertex <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
