<p id="S3.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p">Note that these pictures are formally similar to (<a href="#S3.E12" title="In 3.3. Graphical depiction of the differential ‣ 3. The weight 2 Getzler-Kapranov graph complex ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">For the boundary class <math id="S3.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{irr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{irr}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi^{*}\delta_{irr}=\delta_{irr}-\psi_{t}-\psi_{t^{\prime}}+\sum_{a}\sum_{{t\in A,t^{\prime}\notin A}}\delta_{a,A}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi^{*}\delta_{irr}=\delta_{irr}-\psi_{t}-\psi_{t^{\prime}}+\sum_{a}\sum_{{t\in A,t^{\prime}\notin A}}\delta_{a,A}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p">This means that the action of the differential <math id="S3.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{loop}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{loop}</annotation></semantics></math> on a <math id="S3.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{irr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{irr}</annotation></semantics></math>-decorated vertex may be depicted graphically as</p>
<table id="S3.Ex46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex46X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
