<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4. </span>Example of a nontrivial cocycle in <math id="S3.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{GK}_{g,n}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖦𝖪</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{GK}_{g,n}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we depict a representative in <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{GK}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖦𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{GK}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of the first nontrivial cohomology class produced by Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 1.2. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>. It lives in <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gr_{2}H^{19}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{8})\cong H^{19}(\mathsf{GK}_{8}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>gr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>19</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>19</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖦𝖪</mi><mn>8</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gr_{2}H^{19}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{8})\cong H^{19}(\mathsf{GK}_{8}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and arises from the subspace <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}H_{c}^{6}({\mathcal{M}}_{3,1})\wedge W_{0}H_{c}^{10}({\mathcal{M}}_{5,1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>6</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>10</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}H_{c}^{6}({\mathcal{M}}_{3,1})\wedge W_{0}H_{c}^{10}({\mathcal{M}}_{5,1})</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}_{8,16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}_{8,16}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A representative is given by</p>
