</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Note that any graph with two or more loops at the special vertex is set to zero by these relations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The differential on <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\mathsf{GK}}{}^{2}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖦𝖪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathsf{GK}}{}^{2}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sum of two parts</p>
<table id="S5.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\delta_{split}+\delta_{res}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\delta_{split}+\delta_{res}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{res}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{res}</annotation></semantics></math> encodes the resolution of <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{2}(\overline{{\mathcal{M}}}_{0,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{2}(\overline{{\mathcal{M}}}_{0,n})</annotation></semantics></math> from Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 3.4. ‣ 3.6. Resolutions of 
          
            
              ⁢
              
                
                H
                2
              
              
                
                
                  (
                  
                    
                    
                      ¯
                      M
                    
                    
                      
                        
                        
                        
                      
                      
                        0
                        ,
                        n
                      
                    
                  
                  ) ‣ 3. The weight 2 Getzler-Kapranov graph complex ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>.
Recall that the resolution is given by</p>
<table id="S5.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{ij}\mapsto\psi_{i}+\psi_{j}-\sum_{i\in S,j\in S^{c}}\delta_{0,S}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{ij}\mapsto\psi_{i}+\psi_{j}-\sum_{i\in S,j\in S^{c}}\delta_{0,S}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p">The differential <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{res}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{res}</annotation></semantics></math> applies this formula to
the <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>-decoration at the special vertex, with a conventional sign <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>e</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{e}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of structural edges. Graphically, this may be depicted as</p>
<table id="S5.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(25)</span></td>
