</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.4" class="ltx_p">If the special vertex is decorated by <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0,A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0,A}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{res}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{res}</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes.
Note that <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{res}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{res}</annotation></semantics></math> is homogeneous of degree 1.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The part <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}</annotation></semantics></math> splits undecorated vertices as usual.
When the special vertex is split this is done as follows:</p>
<ul id="S5.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If decorated by <math id="S5.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> the special vertex is again split as in (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In 3.3. Graphical depiction of the differential ‣ 3. The weight 2 Getzler-Kapranov graph complex ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) on p. <a href="#S3.E13" title="In 3.3. Graphical depiction of the differential ‣ 3. The weight 2 Getzler-Kapranov graph complex ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If decorated by <math id="S5.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0,S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0,S}</annotation></semantics></math> the special vertex is split as in (<a href="#S3.E14" title="In 3.3. Graphical depiction of the differential ‣ 3. The weight 2 Getzler-Kapranov graph complex ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) on p. <a href="#S3.E14" title="In 3.3. Graphical depiction of the differential ‣ 3. The weight 2 Getzler-Kapranov graph complex ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If decorated by <math id="S5.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> some subset <math id="S5.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> of half-edges is split off that does not contain both <math id="S5.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.I4.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> (but might contain neither of them), as shown:</p>
<table id="S5.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(26)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
