<p id="S5.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">The first term in (<a href="#S5.E27" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.2. A resolution of 
          
            
              ¯
              GK
            
            
              2
            
            
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  g
                  ,
                  n ‣ 5. A zig-zag of quasi-isomorphisms of graph complexes ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) agrees with that in (<a href="#S5.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.2. A resolution of 
          
            
              ¯
              GK
            
            
              2
            
            
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  g
                  ,
                  n ‣ 5. A zig-zag of quasi-isomorphisms of graph complexes ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), with the sign due to interchanging the two edges. The second term agrees with the second term in (<a href="#S5.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.2. A resolution of 
          
            
              ¯
              GK
            
            
              2
            
            
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  g
                  ,
                  n ‣ 5. A zig-zag of quasi-isomorphisms of graph complexes ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) due to the relations. Each summand in the third term appears twice, with opposite sign, by applying <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}</annotation></semantics></math> to two different terms in the sum appearing in (<a href="#S5.E24" title="In 5.2. A resolution of 
          
            
              ¯
              GK
            
            
              2
            
            
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  g
                  ,
                  n ‣ 5. A zig-zag of quasi-isomorphisms of graph complexes ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>).
The verification that the differential respects the fourth loop relation is similar.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we must check that the differential squares to zero. Suppose <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a generator for <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\mathsf{GK}}{}^{2}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖦𝖪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathsf{GK}}{}^{2}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. We must show:</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\delta_{split}+\delta_{res})^{2}\Gamma=\delta_{split}^{2}\Gamma+(\delta_{split}\delta_{res}+\delta_{res}\delta_{split})\Gamma=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\delta_{split}+\delta_{res})^{2}\Gamma=\delta_{split}^{2}\Gamma+(\delta_{split}\delta_{res}+\delta_{res}\delta_{split})\Gamma=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">The argument for cancellation of terms that arise from splitting non-special vertices is identical to the proof that differential squares to zero on the ordinary commutative graph complex. The same argument adapts easily to cases where the special vertex is decorated with <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0,A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0,A}</annotation></semantics></math>, because in these cases <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{res}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{res}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose the special vertex is decorated by <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The standard argument shows that <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}^{2}\Gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}^{2}\Gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math>. It remains to show <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\delta_{split}\delta_{res}+\delta_{res}\delta_{split})\Gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\delta_{split}\delta_{res}+\delta_{res}\delta_{split})\Gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{res}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{res}</annotation></semantics></math> to the right-hand side of (<a href="#S5.E26" title="In 3rd item ‣ 5.2. A resolution of 
          
            
              ¯
              GK
            
            
              2
            
            
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  g
                  ,
                  n ‣ 5. A zig-zag of quasi-isomorphisms of graph complexes ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) gives <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{e+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{e+1}</annotation></semantics></math> times</span></p>
<table id="S5.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(29)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}\sum\,\hbox to33.55pt{\vbox to34.25pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 21.25621pt\lower-9.55789pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin} {{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}}
