<p id="S5.I5.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In both cases (<a href="#S5.E32" title="In 3rd item ‣ 5.3. Completing the zig-zag ‣ 5. A zig-zag of quasi-isomorphisms of graph complexes ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) and (<a href="#S5.E33" title="In 3rd item ‣ 5.3. Completing the zig-zag ‣ 5. A zig-zag of quasi-isomorphisms of graph complexes ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>), <math id="S5.I5.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> has one more edge than <math id="S5.I5.i3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. We may assume, without loss of generality, that the decorated edge (of which <math id="S5.I5.i3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is one half-edge) is the first in the ordering of edges. Then we order the structural edges in <math id="S5.I5.i3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> such that the edge containing <math id="S5.I5.i3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is first, the edge containing the opposite half-edge of <math id="S5.I5.i3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is second, and the relative order of the remaining edges is unchanged.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.4</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The map <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is a map of complexes.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is clear that the map <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> respects the degrees and genera and is hence a well-defined map of graded vector spaces. We need to verify that it commutes with the differentials,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\Phi(\Gamma)=\Phi(\delta\Gamma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\Phi(\Gamma)=\Phi(\delta\Gamma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that the differential on <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\mathsf{GK}}{}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖦𝖪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathsf{GK}}{}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\delta_{split}+\delta_{res}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\delta_{split}+\delta_{res}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the differential on <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We furthermore decompose the operation <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\mathsf{GK}}{}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖦𝖪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathsf{GK}}{}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> into two terms,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}=\delta_{split}^{s}+\delta_{split}^{o}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>o</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}=\delta_{split}^{s}+\delta_{split}^{o},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> splitting the special vertex and <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}^{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>o</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}^{o}</annotation></semantics></math> the other vertices.
Similarly, we write <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}\Phi(\Gamma)=(\delta_{split}^{s}+\delta_{split}^{o})\Phi(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>o</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}\Phi(\Gamma)=(\delta_{split}^{s}+\delta_{split}^{o})\Phi(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> splitting the vertex that is the image of the special vertex, when the decoration on <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}^{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>o</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}^{o}</annotation></semantics></math> splitting the other vertices. (When the decoration on <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, we set <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}^{s}\Phi(\Gamma)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}^{s}\Phi(\Gamma)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.)
Since away from the special vertex the graph is not altered by <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(\delta_{split}^{o}\Gamma)=\delta_{split}^{o}\Phi(\Gamma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>o</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>o</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\delta_{split}^{o}\Gamma)=\delta_{split}^{o}\Phi(\Gamma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Keep in mind that if <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> has a <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>-decoration then <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> has one more structural edge than <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, producing an additional <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math> sign upon applying <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}^{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>o</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}^{o}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, due to the sign <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>e</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{e}</annotation></semantics></math> in the definition of <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> the signs on both sides of the above equation still agree.
Next, we then need to check that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\delta_{split}^{s}+\delta_{join})\Phi(\Gamma)=\Phi((\delta_{split}^{s}+\delta_{res})\Gamma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\delta_{split}^{s}+\delta_{join})\Phi(\Gamma)=\Phi((\delta_{split}^{s}+\delta_{res})\Gamma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">We consider cases according to the decoration at the special vertex of <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, suppose that the special vertex of <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is decorated by <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0,A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0,A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(\Gamma)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\Gamma)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{res}\Gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{res}\Gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so we need to check that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(\delta_{split}^{s}\Gamma)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\delta_{split}^{s}\Gamma)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The only terms of <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}^{s}\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}^{s}\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> that do not themselves carry a <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-decoration (and are hence sent to zero by <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>) are those appearing in the last line of (<a href="#S3.E14" title="In 3.3. Graphical depiction of the differential ‣ 3. The weight 2 Getzler-Kapranov graph complex ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) on p. <a href="#S3.E14" title="In 3.3. Graphical depiction of the differential ‣ 3. The weight 2 Getzler-Kapranov graph complex ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>. Both of these terms are mapped to the same graph via <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> as depicted in (<a href="#S5.E32" title="In 3rd item ‣ 5.3. Completing the zig-zag ‣ 5. A zig-zag of quasi-isomorphisms of graph complexes ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>), with opposite orderings of the two <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-edges, and hence the matching terms cancel.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, suppose that the special vertex of <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is decorated by <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We have <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{res}\Gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{res}\Gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and, since <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> has no <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-legs, <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{join}\Phi(\Gamma)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{join}\Phi(\Gamma)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We need to check that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}^{s}\Phi(\Gamma)=\Phi(\delta_{split}^{s}\Gamma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}^{s}\Phi(\Gamma)=\Phi(\delta_{split}^{s}\Gamma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the definitions shows that both sides have the same form</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

