<p id="S5.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">This cannot produce a “forbidden graph” with decoration <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{it}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{it}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{tt^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{tt^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are the half-edges of a loop, because, in defining <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we excluded graphs with <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon,\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon,\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>- and <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\omega,\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\omega,\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>-edges. By construction, <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(\widetilde{\Gamma})=\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\widetilde{\Gamma})=\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to consider the case where <math id="S5.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> has no <math id="S5.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorated external vertices.
Then we build <math id="S5.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> by deleting the two <math id="S5.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-decorated external vertices and their incident legs, joining the two unpaired half-edges into a new edge, and adding a <math id="S5.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>-decoration on one of the two, as shown.</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

