<p id="S6.SS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\geq 2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\geq 2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>) spanned by graphs that have 1 (resp. <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>) <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorations in <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-components.
Using again Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2.2. Quasi-isomorphisms and acyclicity ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> it suffices to check that the map (part of the differential <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{join}^{\epsilon,\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{join}^{\epsilon,\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\geq 2}^{\prime}\to W_{1}^{\prime}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\geq 2}^{\prime}\to W_{1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">is an isomorphism. Combinatorially, this map joins all <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorated external vertices in <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-components, attaching a new internal vertex together with an <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-leg:</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
