<p id="S6.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The structural edges of each graph in <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{S}(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{S}(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> are in bijection with those of <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, and we keep the given ordering.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 6.6</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The restriction on the union of all <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-components of graphs in <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\star}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\star}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> (Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm2" title="Definition 6.2. ‣ 6.1. A quasi-isomorphic subcomplex ‣ 6. A quasi-isomorphic subcomplex ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a>) guarantees that the reattachment operation does not produce connected components without any <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>- or <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-decoration. For this reason, <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined on <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\star}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\star}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is not well-defined on <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now consider the graded endomorphism <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\star}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\star}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>, given by</p>
<table id="S6.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi(\Gamma)=(-1)^{\#\epsilon}\sum_{S}R_{S}(\Gamma)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>S</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi(\Gamma)=(-1)^{\#\epsilon}\sum_{S}R_{S}(\Gamma),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the sum runs over all subsets of the set of <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorations, and <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorations in <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.7</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The map <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi</annotation></semantics></math> is an involution, i.e., it is invertible and <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi^{-1}=\Xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi^{-1}=\Xi</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Any graph appearing in <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi\circ\Xi\,(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi\circ\Xi\,(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by reattaching some subset <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> of the <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorated legs to internal vertices. Each such graph appears <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{|S|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{|S|}</annotation></semantics></math> different ways, with signs that cancel unless <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\in X^{\star}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\in X^{\star}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> a graph, <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> a non-empty subset of its <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorated external vertices and <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{S}^{j}(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{S}^{j}(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>
be the graph obtained by reattaching the external vertices in <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to the midpoint of the edge that contains the <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> decoration.</p>
