\lxSVG@closescope }}}
\lxSVG@closescope {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This operation creates precisely one new structural edge, which we take to be first in the ordering, preserving the relative ordering of the remaining edges.
Note that the operation also makes sense if applied not to a numbered leg, but an <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-labeled leg, and we shall denote the sum of such operations applied to the two <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-legs by <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{S}^{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>ω</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{S}^{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We also define</p>
<table id="S6.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\delta}_{join}^{j}(\Gamma)=\sum_{|S|\geq 1}|\,S|\cdot R_{S}^{j}(\Gamma)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\delta}_{join}^{j}(\Gamma)=\sum_{|S|\geq 1}|\,S|\cdot R_{S}^{j}(\Gamma),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where the sum runs over all non-empty subsets of the set of <math id="S6.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-legs of <math id="S6.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then have the following result:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 6.8</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\delta}:=\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}-\sum_{j=1}^{n}\tilde{\delta}_{join}^{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\delta}:=\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}-\sum_{j=1}^{n}\tilde{\delta}_{join}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\delta}=\Xi\circ\delta\circ\Xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\delta}=\Xi\circ\delta\circ\Xi</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi</annotation></semantics></math> defines an isomorphism of dg vector spaces</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi\colon(X^{\star}_{g,n},\tilde{\delta})\to(X^{\star}_{g,n},\delta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi\colon(X^{\star}_{g,n},\tilde{\delta})\to(X^{\star}_{g,n},\delta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is similar to that of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>, Lemma 3.6]</cite>; the argument there goes through essentially unchanged, even though the complexes <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\star}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\star}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> we consider here are different. We give only a condensed sketch of the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We introduce the following notation. For <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> a subset of the <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-legs in some graph <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\in X^{\star}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\in X^{\star}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> we denote by <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{S}^{\epsilon}(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{S}^{\epsilon}(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> the graph obtained by reattaching the legs in <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to a new <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorated vertex.</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{S}^{\epsilon}\colon\hbox to28.85pt{\vbox to48.85pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 14.42638pt\lower-30.77098pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin} 
{{}}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\hbox{\hbox{{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin} {{}{{{}}}{{}}{}{}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{}{}{}{}{}{{}\lxSVG@stroke\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 12.92 11.81 C 12.92 18.95 7.14 24.73 0 24.73 C -7.14 24.73 -12.92 18.95 -12.92 11.81 C -12.92 4.67 -7.14 -1.11 0 -1.11 C 7.14 -1.11 12.92 4.67 12.92 11.81 Z M 0 11.81}{fill:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
}{{{{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}}\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin} \lxSVG@transformcm{1.0}{0.0}{0.0}{1.0}{-3.125pt}{5.11925pt}\lxSVG@begingroup@{transform} \pgfsys@hbox{58}\lxSVG@closescope }}}
