<p id="S6.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, we denote by <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}_{S}(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}_{S}(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> the sum of graphs obtained from <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{S}^{\epsilon}(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{S}^{\epsilon}(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> by attaching the newly formed <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-leg to an internal vertex of <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
