<p id="S6.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using the fact that <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi^{-1}=\Xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi^{-1}=\Xi</annotation></semantics></math>, one computes that</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Xi\circ\delta_{split}\circ\Xi)(\Gamma)=\delta_{split}(\Gamma)+\sum_{|S|\geq 2}|S|\cdot R_{S}^{\epsilon}(\Gamma)+\sum_{|S|\geq 2}(|S|-1)\cdot R^{\prime}_{S}(\Gamma)+\sum_{|S|\geq 1}\sum_{j\in\{1,\dots,n,\omega\}}R_{S}^{j}(\Gamma)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Xi\circ\delta_{split}\circ\Xi)(\Gamma)=\delta_{split}(\Gamma)+\sum_{|S|\geq 2}|S|\cdot R_{S}^{\epsilon}(\Gamma)+\sum_{|S|\geq 2}(|S|-1)\cdot R^{\prime}_{S}(\Gamma)+\sum_{|S|\geq 1}\sum_{j\in\{1,\dots,n,\omega\}}R_{S}^{j}(\Gamma),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> runs over subsets of the set of <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-legs.
Similarly, one may compute</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Xi\circ\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}\circ\Xi)(\Gamma)=\sum_{|S|\geq 2}(1-|S|)\cdot R_{S}^{\epsilon}(\Gamma)+\sum_{|S|\geq 2}(1-|S|)\cdot R^{\prime}_{S}(\Gamma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Xi\circ\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}\circ\Xi)(\Gamma)=\sum_{|S|\geq 2}(1-|S|)\cdot R_{S}^{\epsilon}(\Gamma)+\sum_{|S|\geq 2}(1-|S|)\cdot R^{\prime}_{S}(\Gamma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Together we find that</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\Xi\circ(\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon})\circ\Xi)(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\Xi\circ(\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon})\circ\Xi)(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex114.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}+\delta_{join}^{\omega})\Gamma+\sum_{|S|\geq 1}\sum_{j\in\{1,\dots,n\}}R_{S}^{j}(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ω</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}+\delta_{join}^{\omega})\Gamma+\sum_{|S|\geq 1}\sum_{j\in\{1,\dots,n\}}R_{S}^{j}(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta(\Gamma)+\sum_{|S|\geq 1}\sum_{j\in\{1,\dots,n\}}R_{S}^{j}(\Gamma)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta(\Gamma)+\sum_{|S|\geq 1}\sum_{j\in\{1,\dots,n\}}R_{S}^{j}(\Gamma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">Then one may finally compute that</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Big(\Xi\circ\sum_{|S|\geq 1}R_{S}^{j}\circ\Xi\Big)\,(\Gamma)=\sum_{|S|\geq 1}|S|\cdot R_{S}^{j}(\Gamma)=\tilde{\delta}_{join}^{j}(\Gamma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">∘</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big(\Xi\circ\sum_{|S|\geq 1}R_{S}^{j}\circ\Xi\Big)\,(\Gamma)=\sum_{|S|\geq 1}|S|\cdot R_{S}^{j}(\Gamma)=\tilde{\delta}_{join}^{j}(\Gamma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.7.1" class="ltx_text">Putting the above computations together we find that</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Xi\circ\tilde{\delta}\circ\Xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Xi\circ\tilde{\delta}\circ\Xi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex117.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Xi\circ\Big(\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}-\sum_{j}\tilde{\delta}_{join}^{j}\Big)\circ\Xi=\delta+\sum_{j}\delta_{join}^{j}-\sum_{j}\delta_{join}^{j}=\delta," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Xi\circ\Big(\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}-\sum_{j}\tilde{\delta}_{join}^{j}\Big)\circ\Xi=\delta+\sum_{j}\delta_{join}^{j}-\sum_{j}\delta_{join}^{j}=\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.8.1" class="ltx_text">which proves the proposition.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7. </span>The weight 2 compactly supported cohomology of <math id="S7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now focus on the special case where <math id="S7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the quasi-isomorphic subcomplex <math id="S7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\star}_{g}\subset X_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\star}_{g}\subset X_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>, with its simplified differential <math id="S7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we shall see that the cohomology of <math id="S7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> can be fully expressed through the cohomology of the ordinary commutative graph complexes <math id="S7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{(g^{\prime},n^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{(g^{\prime},n^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math> of Section <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>, with <math id="S7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}=1,2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}=g,g-1,g-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}=g,g-1,g-2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the differential <math id="S7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> in Proposition <a href="#S6.Thmthm8" title="Proposition 6.8. ‣ 6.2. A simplifying involution ‣ 6. A quasi-isomorphic subcomplex ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.8</span></a> further simplifies to
<math id="S7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define the subcomplex</p>
<table id="S7.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(36)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g}\subset(X^{\star}_{g},\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g}\subset(X^{\star}_{g},\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p2.2" class="ltx_p">spanned by graphs with either no <math id="S7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorations, or exactly two on an <math id="S7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon,\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon,\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-edge. Note that <math id="S7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes on <math id="S7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We also introduce the space</p>
<table id="S7.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{(\bullet,n)}=\bigoplus_{g}G^{(g,n)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mi>g</mi></munder><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{(\bullet,n)}=\bigoplus_{g}G^{(g,n)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p3.2" class="ltx_p">that inherits an additional grading by the genus.
We also define the exterior product</p>
<table id="S7.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}_{\bullet}=\bigwedge^{2}G^{(\bullet,1)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕎</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mn>2</mn></mover><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}_{\bullet}=\bigwedge^{2}G^{(\bullet,1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p3.3" class="ltx_p">This comes with a grading inherited from the genus grading; let <math id="S7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> be the homogeneous part of genus <math id="S7.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.1</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The subspace <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>
is a subcomplex with respect to <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\delta}=\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\delta}=\delta_{split}+\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H_{g},\tilde{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H_{g},\tilde{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math> is isomorphic to</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}_{g}[-3]\oplus G^{(g-1,2)}_{as}[-3]\oplus\mathbb{W}_{g-1}[-4]\oplus G^{(g-2,2)}_{as}[-4]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕎</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}_{g}[-3]\oplus G^{(g-1,2)}_{as}[-3]\oplus\mathbb{W}_{g-1}[-4]\oplus G^{(g-2,2)}_{as}[-4].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Here the subscript <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-)_{as}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-)_{as}</annotation></semantics></math> refers to taking the antisymmetric part under the <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-action permuting the labels <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Graphs in <math id="S7.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> have exactly two <math id="S7.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-decorated legs, and every connected component has an <math id="S7.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>- or <math id="S7.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorated leg. There are four possibilities, with and without an <math id="S7.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon,\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon,\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-edge, and with 1 or 2 <math id="S7.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-components:</span></p>
