<p id="S7.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The graded vector space <math id="S7.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> decomposes into a direct sum of 4 subcomplexes accordingly; these subcomplexes are identified with <math id="S7.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}_{g}[-3]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}_{g}[-3]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{(g-1,2)}_{as}[-3]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{(g-1,2)}_{as}[-3]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}_{g-1}[-4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕎</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}_{g-1}[-4]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S7.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{(g-2,2)}_{as}[-4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{(g-2,2)}_{as}[-4]</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, since <math id="S7.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{join}^{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes on <math id="S7.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 7.2</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The inclusion (<a href="#S7.E36" title="In 7. The weight 2 compactly supported cohomology of 
        
          
            
            M
            g ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>) is a quasi-isomorphism.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
