<p id="S7.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">with the graded subspace <math id="S7.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}\subset U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}\subset U</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S7.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\geq 2}\subset U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\geq 2}\subset U</annotation></semantics></math>) being spanned by graphs with exactly <math id="S7.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> (respectively <math id="S7.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>) <math id="S7.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-legs.
The drawn arrows indicate various parts of the differential.
In particular, the part</span></p>
