<div id="S7.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">This part is injective, since the operation can be undone by removing the two newly added vertices, and adding back the <math id="S7.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorations on legs.
By Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2.2. Quasi-isomorphisms and acyclicity ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> we hence conclude that the projection</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\to\coker D" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>coker</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\to\coker D</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">is a quasi-isomorphism.
The cokernel of <math id="S7.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is spanned by graphs in <math id="S7.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the unique <math id="S7.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-leg is connected to a vertex <math id="S7.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> that is connected to an <math id="S7.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-leg. (Recall that we forbade <math id="S7.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon,\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon,\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>-edges in the definition of <math id="S7.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>.)</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
