<p id="S7.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="S7.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S7.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>) being spanned by graphs for which the vertex <math id="S7.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> has valence <math id="S7.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S7.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>).
The part of the differential</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex132" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}:U_{2}^{\prime}\to U_{1}^{\prime}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}:U_{2}^{\prime}\to U_{1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">is injective. Hence, applying Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2.2. Quasi-isomorphisms and acyclicity ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> again, we find that the projection</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\coker(D)\to\coker(D^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>coker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>coker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\coker(D)\to\coker(D^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p9.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p9.6.1" class="ltx_text">is a quasi-isomorphism.
The cokernel of <math id="S7.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is spanned by graphs in <math id="S7.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the unique vertex <math id="S7.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> neighboring <math id="S7.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> has an <math id="S7.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-hair attached.</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
