<p id="S8.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S8.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a (possibly disconnected) generator for <math id="S8.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the lemma follows.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We remark that the identification <math id="S8.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g,1}\cong H_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g,1}\cong H_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> of the lemma is induced by the pullback under the forgetful map <math id="S8.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,1}\to\overline{{\mathcal{M}}}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,1}\to\overline{{\mathcal{M}}}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>, see Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1. The pullback map ‣ Appendix A A direct map 
        
          X
          
            
              
                
                
                
              
              
                g
                ,
                n
              
            
          
          →
          
            ¯
            GK
          
          
            
              
                
                
                
              
              
                g
                ,
                n
              
            
          
          
            2 ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> below.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Combining Lemmas <a href="#S7.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 7.1. ‣ 7. The weight 2 compactly supported cohomology of 
        
          
            
            M
            g ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a> and <a href="#S8.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 8.3. ‣ 8.1. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              H
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  g
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.3</span></a>, we can express the cohomology of <math id="S8.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> through the graph cohomology <math id="S8.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(G^{(g^{\prime},n^{\prime})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(G^{(g^{\prime},n^{\prime})})</annotation></semantics></math>, or equivalently through <math id="S8.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}H_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g^{\prime},n^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}H_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g^{\prime},n^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.2. </span>The graphs in <math id="S8.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
