</div>
<div id="S8.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now compute the cohomology of <math id="S8.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\star}_{0,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\star}_{0,n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S8.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 8.4</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(J^{\star}_{0,n},\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(J^{\star}_{0,n},\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> has dimension <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-2)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-2)!</annotation></semantics></math> and is concentrated in degree <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
More precisely, there is an isomorphism of <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{n-1}(J^{\star}_{0,n},\delta)\cong H_{c}^{n-3}({\mathcal{M}}_{0,n})\cong\mathsf{Lie}((n))\otimes\sgn_{n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>sgn</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{n-1}(J^{\star}_{0,n},\delta)\cong H_{c}^{n-3}({\mathcal{M}}_{0,n})\cong\mathsf{Lie}((n))\otimes\sgn_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
