<p id="S8.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">The differential is then given by</span></p>
<table id="S8.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(39)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F_{1},\dots,F_{n})\to\sum_{j=1}^{n}[x_{j},F_{j}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F_{1},\dots,F_{n})\to\sum_{j=1}^{n}[x_{j},F_{j}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is surjective, as required.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the second statement of Proposition <a href="#S8.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 8.4. ‣ 8.3. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  0
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.4</span></a> we take for granted the well-known fact that <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{c}^{n-3}({\mathcal{M}}_{0,n})\cong\mathsf{Lie}((n))\otimes\sgn_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>sgn</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{c}^{n-3}({\mathcal{M}}_{0,n})\cong\mathsf{Lie}((n))\otimes\sgn_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
It then remains to check that the kernel of (<a href="#S8.E39" title="In Proof. ‣ 8.3. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  0
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) can be identified with <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Lie}((n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Lie}((n))</annotation></semantics></math> as an <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-module.
We may do this by providng an injective map</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota:\mathsf{Lie}((n))\to\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota:\mathsf{Lie}((n))\to\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">whose image is in the kernel of (<a href="#S8.E39" title="In Proof. ‣ 8.3. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  0
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>).
To construct <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ι</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the following notation
for elements of <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Lie}((n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Lie}((n))</annotation></semantics></math>.
We have that <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Lie}((n))\cong\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Lie}((n))\cong\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})</annotation></semantics></math>
and we write</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x_{1},\dots,x_{n}):=\langle f_{n}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1}),x_{n}\rangle\in\mathsf{Lie}((n))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x_{1},\dots,x_{n}):=\langle f_{n}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1}),x_{n}\rangle\in\mathsf{Lie}((n))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">for the element corresponding to a Lie expression <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})\in\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})\in\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-action on <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Lie}((n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Lie}((n))</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by permuting variables, considering <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle-,-\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle-,-\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> formally as an invariant inner product.
In particular, for each <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> we have Lie expressions
<math id="S8.SS3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})\in\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})\in\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})=\langle f_{j}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n}),x_{j}\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})=\langle f_{j}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n}),x_{j}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">We then define the map <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ι</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex151" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota(f):=(f_{1},f_{2},\dots,f_{n})\in\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota(f):=(f_{1},f_{2},\dots,f_{n})\in\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">It is clear that <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ι</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota</annotation></semantics></math> is an injection since <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> may be recovered from any of the <math id="S8.SS3.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We are hence left with checking that the composition of <math id="S8.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ι</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href="#S8.E39" title="In Proof. ‣ 8.3. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  0
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) is zero.
To this end, note that in <math id="S8.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Lie}((n+1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Lie}((n+1))</annotation></semantics></math> we have the equality</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex152"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle[x_{j},f_{j}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})],x_{n+1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle[x_{j},f_{j}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})],x_{n+1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex152.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\langle f_{j}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n}),[x_{j},x_{n+1}]\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\langle f_{j}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n}),[x_{j},x_{n+1}]\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f(x_{1},\dots,[x_{n+1},x_{j}],\dots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(x_{1},\dots,[x_{n+1},x_{j}],\dots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle f_{n}(x_{1},\dots,[x_{n+1},x_{j}],\dots,x_{n-1}),x_{n}\rangle," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle f_{n}(x_{1},\dots,[x_{n+1},x_{j}],\dots,x_{n-1}),x_{n}\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="S8.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\dots,n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\dots,n-1</annotation></semantics></math>, using invariance of our formal inner product <math id="S8.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle-,-\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle-,-\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and the definition of the <math id="S8.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus in <math id="S8.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Lie}((n+1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Lie}((n+1))</annotation></semantics></math> we have that</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex155"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\sum_{j=1}^{n}[x_{j},f_{j}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})],x_{n+1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\sum_{j=1}^{n}[x_{j},f_{j}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})],x_{n+1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex156"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle-[x_{n+1},f_{n}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})]+\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}f_{n}(x_{1},\dots,[x_{n+1},x_{j}],\dots,x_{n-1}),x_{n}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle-[x_{n+1},f_{n}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})]+\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}f_{n}(x_{1},\dots,[x_{n+1},x_{j}],\dots,x_{n-1}),x_{n}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">by the Jacobi identity.
Hence <math id="S8.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{n}[x_{j},f_{j}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{n}[x_{j},f_{j}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})]=0</annotation></semantics></math> as desired and the second statement of Proposition <a href="#S8.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 8.4. ‣ 8.3. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  0
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.4</span></a> follows.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The second statement of Proposition <a href="#S8.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 8.4. ‣ 8.3. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  0
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.4</span></a> was kindly pointed out to us by the anonymous referee, whom we thank for her or his contribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_ex">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 8.5</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, Proposition <a href="#S8.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 8.4. ‣ 8.3. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  0
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.4</span></a> states that <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(J^{\star}_{0,2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(J^{\star}_{0,2})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional, concentrated in degree <math id="S8.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Tracing the proof, one can see that a representative is given by the cocycle</p>
