<section id="S8.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.4. </span>The cohomology of <math id="S8.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\star}_{1,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\star}_{1,n}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S8.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each generator for <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\star}_{1,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\star}_{1,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has one of six combinatorial types: with or without an <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon,j)</annotation></semantics></math>-edge, and with 0, 1, or 2 other <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorations. The following diagram depicts one generator of each type (for varying values of <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>). We denote the corresponding graded subspaces of <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\star}_{1,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\star}_{1,n}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,k}</annotation></semantics></math>, as shown. The notation is chosen so that a generator for <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,k}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-k</annotation></semantics></math> edges of type <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon,j)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2-i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2-i</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-decorations on other componentss.</p>
