<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(\tilde{V}_{1,1},\tilde{\delta}_{split})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(\tilde{V}_{1,1},\tilde{\delta}_{split})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cong\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})[-n-2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖠𝗌𝗌𝗈𝖼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cong\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})[-n-2]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(42)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(\tilde{V}_{2,1},\tilde{\delta}_{split})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(\tilde{V}_{2,1},\tilde{\delta}_{split})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cong\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})_{\mathbb{S}_{2}}[-n-3]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠𝗌𝗌𝗈𝖼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cong\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})_{\mathbb{S}_{2}}[-n-3].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S8.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠𝗌𝗌𝗈𝖼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is the subspace of the free associative algebra spanned by words in which each variable appears exactly once, and <math id="S8.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> acts by reversing each word (corresponding to the symmetry reversing the orientation of a based loop).
Under the identification (<a href="#S8.E41" title="In 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), the associative word <math id="S8.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1}\cdots x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}\cdots x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the graph</p>
