<p id="S8.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p">The cohomology groups in the second row of (<a href="#S8.E40" title="In 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>) are similar, but one must take a direct sum over the decorations <math id="S8.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> that appears in an <math id="S8.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon,j)</annotation></semantics></math>-edge, and omit the variable <math id="S8.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S8.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\tilde{V}_{0,0},\delta_{split})\cong\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})[-n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\tilde{V}_{0,0},\delta_{split})\cong\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})[-n]</annotation></semantics></math>, and so on.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">With these identifications, the <math id="S8.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-page of our spectral sequence (see diagram (<a href="#S8.E40" title="In 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>)) hence becomes isomorphic to the total complex of the following diagram, from which we omit degree shifts for notational brevity:<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            The bottom left space is concentrated in degree <math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, and each arrow increases the degree by one.</span></span></span></p>
<table id="S8.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(43)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="S8.E43.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:494.4pt;height:60.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<div id="S8.E43.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:304.8pt;height:39.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-82.1pt,10.5pt) scale(0.7,0.7) ;">
<p id="S8.E43.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.E43.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S8.E43.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="83.21" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-41.61px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 639.54 83.21" width="639.54"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,83.21) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(319.77,0) translate(0,41.61)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -319.77 -22.71)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 83.21)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 15.44)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 34.55 0) translate(52.85,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -46.89 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="79.95"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.E43.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 209.36 0) translate(94.23,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -55.06 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.96em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="96.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.E43.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠𝗌𝗌𝗈𝖼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 435.63 0) translate(100.33,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -61.16 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.84em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="108.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.E43.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})_{\mathbb{S}_{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠𝗌𝗌𝗈𝖼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})_{\mathbb{S}_{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 64.31)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(87.4,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -81.44 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:1em;font-size:10pt;" height="24.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="149.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.E43.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 174.8 0) translate(128.78,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -89.61 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:11.95em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:1em;font-size:10pt;" height="24.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="165.39"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.E43.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖠𝗌𝗌𝗈𝖼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 399.15 0) translate(136.8,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -97.63 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:13.11em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:1em;font-size:10pt;" height="24.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="181.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S8.E43.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})_{\mathbb{S}_{2}}.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖠𝗌𝗌𝗈𝖼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})_{\mathbb{S}_{2}}.}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -179.24 29.62 L -78.04 29.62"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -77.76 29.62)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 45.1 29.62 L 148.23 29.62"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 148.51 29.62)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -144.69 -19.25 L -112.59 -19.25"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -112.31 -19.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -232.37 -6.99 L -232.37 16.81"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 -232.37 17.09)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 79.65 -19.25 L 111.76 -19.25"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 112.03 -19.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -16.19 -6.99 L -16.19 16.81"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 -16.19 17.09)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 216.18 -6.99 L 216.18 16.81"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 216.18 17.09)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g></g></svg></span></span></p>
</span></div>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Each vertical arrow in (<a href="#S8.E43" title="In 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) is defined by the formula</p>
<table id="S8.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(44)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F_{1},\dots,F_{n})\mapsto\sum_{j=1}^{n}[x_{j},F_{j}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F_{1},\dots,F_{n})\mapsto\sum_{j=1}^{n}[x_{j},F_{j}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p">The horizontal arrows are the canonical inclusions and projections, so that the cohomology of each row of (<a href="#S8.E43" title="In 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) is concentrated in the middle term. It is hence easy to check (for example, using Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2.2. Quasi-isomorphisms and acyclicity ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> again) that the total complex of (<a href="#S8.E43" title="In 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) is quasi-isomorphic to the two-term complex built from its row-wise cohomology.
It hence remains to study these middle cohomology groups of each row, and the induced map between them.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">To this end let <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{Pois}}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{Pois}}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> be the part of the free Poisson algebra in <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> in which each <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> appears exactly once.
Its elements are linear combinations of Poisson expressions of the form</p>
<table id="S8.Ex163" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})=f_{1}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\wedge\cdots\wedge f_{k}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∧</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})=f_{1}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\wedge\cdots\wedge f_{k}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p">where the <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are Lie words, such that each variable <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> appears exactly once in <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{Pois}}^{k}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{Pois}}^{k}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> be the subspace spanned by expressions that are products of exactly <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> Lie words. There is a natural map</p>
<table id="S8.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(45)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{k}:\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}{\mathsf{Pois}}^{k}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})\to{\mathsf{Pois}}^{k}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{k}:\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}{\mathsf{Pois}}^{k}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})\to{\mathsf{Pois}}^{k}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS4.p7.3" class="ltx_p">given again by the expression (<a href="#S8.E44" title="In 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>), i.e.,
<math id="S8.SS4.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F_{1},\dots,F_{n})\mapsto\sum_{j=1}^{n}[x_{j},F_{j}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F_{1},\dots,F_{n})\mapsto\sum_{j=1}^{n}[x_{j},F_{j}].</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us define</p>
<table id="S8.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex164"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{A}_{n}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{A}_{n}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex164.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\ker D_{n}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\ker D_{n}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex164.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{B}_{n}^{k}:=\coker D_{n}^{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>coker</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{B}_{n}^{k}:=\coker D_{n}^{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS4.p7.4" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S8.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(46)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{A}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{A}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\bigoplus_{j\geq 1}\mathbb{A}_{n}^{2j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\bigoplus_{j\geq 1}\mathbb{A}_{n}^{2j+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E46.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{B}_{n}:=\bigoplus_{j\geq 1}\mathbb{B}_{n}^{2j+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{B}_{n}:=\bigoplus_{j\geq 1}\mathbb{B}_{n}^{2j+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS4.p7.5" class="ltx_p">All objects here are naturally <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-representations, by changing the variable indices and order of summands on the left-hand side of (<a href="#S8.E45" title="In 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>). For example, we have <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{1}=\mathbb{B}_{1}=\mathbb{A}_{2}=\mathbb{B}_{2}=\mathbb{A}_{3}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{1}=\mathbb{B}_{1}=\mathbb{A}_{2}=\mathbb{B}_{2}=\mathbb{A}_{3}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> are one-dimensional trivial representations, and <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> is a three-dimensional irreducible representation of <math id="S8.SS4.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 8.6</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have <math id="S8.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\star}_{1,0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\star}_{1,0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S8.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> we have an isomorphism of graded <math id="S8.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex165" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(J^{\star}_{1,n},\delta)\cong(\mathbb{A}_{n}[-n-1]\oplus\mathbb{B}_{n}[-n-2])\otimes\sgn_{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>sgn</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(J^{\star}_{1,n},\delta)\cong(\mathbb{A}_{n}[-n-1]\oplus\mathbb{B}_{n}[-n-2])\otimes\sgn_{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Equivalently, we must show that <math id="S8.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\tilde{J}^{\star}_{1,n},\tilde{\delta})\cong\mathbb{A}_{n}[-n-1]\oplus\mathbb{B}_{n}[-n-2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\tilde{J}^{\star}_{1,n},\tilde{\delta})\cong\mathbb{A}_{n}[-n-1]\oplus\mathbb{B}_{n}[-n-2]</annotation></semantics></math>. Poincaré-Birkhoff-Witt gives an <math id="S8.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant isomorphism <math id="S8.SS4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{Pois}}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\cong\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠𝗌𝗌𝗈𝖼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{Pois}}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\cong\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying this to the center and righthand columns of (<a href="#S8.E43" title="In 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>),
we get the diagram</span></p>
<table id="S8.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(47)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="S8.E47.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:481.0pt;height:60.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<div id="S8.E47.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:296.0pt;height:39.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-79.7pt,10.5pt) scale(0.7,0.7) ;">
