<p id="S8.SS4.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">The vertical arrows in (<a href="#S8.E47" title="In Proof. ‣ 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>) are still given by (<a href="#S8.E44" title="In 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>).
Furthermore, note that taking <math id="S8.SS4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-coinvariants in the right-hand column is the same is reducing to Poisson words containing evenly many Lie words, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{Pois}}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})_{\mathbb{S}_{2}}\cong\bigoplus_{j&gt;0}{\mathsf{Pois}}^{2j}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{Pois}}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})_{\mathbb{S}_{2}}\cong\bigoplus_{j&gt;0}{\mathsf{Pois}}^{2j}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then the total complex of (<a href="#S8.E47" title="In Proof. ‣ 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>) is quasi-isomorphic to the complex of its row-wise cohomology groups</span></p>
