</table>
<p id="S8.SS4.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">The cohomology of (<a href="#S8.E48" title="In Proof. ‣ 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) is the kernel plus the cokernel of the differential <math id="S8.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}D_{n}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}D_{n}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the direct sum of <math id="S8.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.SS4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, as defined above. The proposition follows, after suitably accounting for the required degree shifts.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The above description of the spaces <math id="S8.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is not very explicit.
However, we can at least provide the following lower bound on the dimensions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8.7</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S8.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex167" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\mathbb{B}_{n}\geq(n-2)!." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\mathbb{B}_{n}\geq(n-2)!.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the definition of <math id="S8.SS4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex168" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="S8.Ex168.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:327.8pt;height:16.7pt;vertical-align:-9.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-17.7pt,0.9pt) scale(0.902318296707968,0.902318296707968) ;">
<p id="S8.Ex168.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.Ex168.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\mathbb{B}_{n}\geq\dim\left(\bigoplus_{k\geq 1}{\mathsf{Pois}}^{2k+1}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\right)-\dim\left(\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\bigoplus_{k\geq 1}{\mathsf{Pois}}^{2k+1}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\mathbb{B}_{n}\geq\dim\left(\bigoplus_{k\geq 1}{\mathsf{Pois}}^{2k+1}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\right)-\dim\left(\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\bigoplus_{k\geq 1}{\mathsf{Pois}}^{2k+1}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS4.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">From the top row of (<a href="#S8.E43" title="In 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<div id="S8.SS4.p11.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:258.8pt;height:26.4pt;vertical-align:-11.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-43.1pt,4.4pt) scale(0.8,0.8) ;">
<div id="S8.SS4.p11.3.1" class="ltx_block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle" style="width:345.0pt;">
<table id="S8.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex169"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dim\left(\bigoplus_{k\geq 1}{\mathsf{Pois}}^{2k+1}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dim\left(\bigoplus_{k\geq 1}{\mathsf{Pois}}^{2k+1}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex169.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dim\left(\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\right)-\dim\left(\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})_{\mathbb{S}_{2}}\right)-\dim\left(\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠𝗌𝗌𝗈𝖼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠𝗌𝗌𝗈𝖼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫𝗂𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dim\left(\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\right)-\dim\left(\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})_{\mathbb{S}_{2}}\right)-\dim\left(\mathsf{Lie}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex170"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=n!-\frac{n!}{2}-(n-1)!," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=n!-\frac{n!}{2}-(n-1)!,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</span></div>
<p id="S8.SS4.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">which simplifies to <math id="S8.SS4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}(n-2)(n-1)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}(n-2)(n-1)!</annotation></semantics></math> Here, we have used that the action of <math id="S8.SS4.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> on associative words of length <math id="S8.SS4.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> is faithful in computing <math id="S8.SS4.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\left(\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})_{\mathbb{S}_{2}}\right)=\frac{n!}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠𝗌𝗌𝗈𝖼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\left(\mathsf{Assoc}(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})_{\mathbb{S}_{2}}\right)=\frac{n!}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the same computation (valid for <math id="S8.SS4.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>) we also see that</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex171"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dim\left(\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\bigoplus_{k\geq 1}{\mathsf{Pois}}^{2k+1}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})\right)=\frac{1}{2}n(n-3)(n-2)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dim\left(\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}\bigoplus_{k\geq 1}{\mathsf{Pois}}^{2k+1}(x_{1},\dots,\hat{x}_{j},\dots,x_{n})\right)=\frac{1}{2}n(n-3)(n-2)!</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS4.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex172" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\mathbb{B}_{n}\geq\frac{1}{2}\left((n-2)(n-1)-n(n-3)\right)(n-2)!," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\mathbb{B}_{n}\geq\frac{1}{2}\left((n-2)(n-1)-n(n-3)\right)(n-2)!,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS4.p11.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p11.6.1" class="ltx_text">which is <math id="S8.SS4.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-2)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-2)!</annotation></semantics></math>, as required.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorems <a href="#S1.Thmthm6" title="Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.6</span></a> and <a href="#S1.Thmthm7" title="Theorem 1.7. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.7</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S8.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#S8.E37" title="In 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>), we know that <math id="S8.SS4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(H_{g,n})\oplus H(J_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(H_{g,n})\oplus H(J_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math> injects into the cohomology of <math id="S8.SS4.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\star}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\star}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. The latter is identified with the cohomology of <math id="S8.SS4.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence with <math id="S8.SS4.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gr_{2}H_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>gr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gr_{2}H_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math>. The summand <math id="S8.SS4.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(H_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(H_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math> is evaluated by Lemma <a href="#S8.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 8.3. ‣ 8.1. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              H
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  g
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.3</span></a>. It contributes only for <math id="S8.SS4.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0,1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0,1</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S8.SS4.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math> it produces an injection of the form (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) on p. <a href="#S1.E3" title="In Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. This injection agrees with the pullback map <math id="S8.SS4.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, as shown in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1. The pullback map ‣ Appendix A A direct map 
        
          X
          
            
              
                
                
                
              
              
                g
                ,
                n
              
            
          
          →
          
            ¯
            GK
          
          
            
              
                
                
                
              
              
                g
                ,
                n
              
            
          
          
            2 ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the summand <math id="S8.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(J_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(J_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math> we can use that by the decomposition (<a href="#S8.E38" title="In 8.2. The graphs in 
          
            
              
              J
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  g
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>) we have an injection of</span></p>
<table id="S8.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(49)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(J^{\star}_{0,n})\otimes H(G^{(g,1)})[-1]\oplus H(J^{\star}_{1,n})\otimes H(G^{(g-1,1)})[-1]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(J^{\star}_{0,n})\otimes H(G^{(g,1)})[-1]\oplus H(J^{\star}_{1,n})\otimes H(G^{(g-1,1)})[-1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS4.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">into its cohomology.
The second factors in the tensor products compute the weight zero cohomology of <math id="S8.SS4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}_{g,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}_{g,1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.SS4.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}_{g-1,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}_{g-1,1}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.
The first factors <math id="S8.SS4.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(J^{\star}_{0,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(J^{\star}_{0,n})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.SS4.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(J^{\star}_{1,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(J^{\star}_{1,n})</annotation></semantics></math> are evaluated by Proposition <a href="#S8.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 8.4. ‣ 8.3. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  0
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.4</span></a> and <a href="#S8.Thmthm6" title="Proposition 8.6. ‣ 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.6</span></a> respectively.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS4.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S8.SS4.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math> one only has a contribution from <math id="S8.SS4.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(J^{\star}_{0,1})\cong\mathbb{Q}[-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(J^{\star}_{0,1})\cong\mathbb{Q}[-1]</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="S8.SS4.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(J^{\star}_{1,1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(J^{\star}_{1,1})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This produces the injection (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) on p. <a href="#S1.E2" title="In Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
To see that this injection indeed corresponds to multiplication with the <math id="S8.SS4.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>-class at the marking as is claimed in Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm6" title="Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.6</span></a> we have to trace the representatives.
Say <math id="S8.SS4.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\in G^{(g,1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\in G^{(g,1)}</annotation></semantics></math> is a cocycle representing a cohomology class in <math id="S8.SS4.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}H_{c}^{k}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}H_{c}^{k}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the corresponding class in <math id="S8.SS4.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(X^{\star}_{g,1},\tilde{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(X^{\star}_{g,1},\tilde{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by</span></p>
