<p id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here “<math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1\leftrightarrow 2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">↔</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1\leftrightarrow 2)</annotation></semantics></math>” stands for the same terms, with the labels 1 and 2 interchanged.
The corresponding cocycle in <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{GK}_{3,2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖦𝖪</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{GK}_{3,2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is then</p>
<table id="S8.Ex177" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
