</table>
<p id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>, we know that <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gr_{2}H_{c}^{\bullet}({\mathcal{M}}_{3,2})\cong\mathbb{Q}\oplus\sgn_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>gr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>sgn</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gr_{2}H_{c}^{\bullet}({\mathcal{M}}_{3,2})\cong\mathbb{Q}\oplus\sgn_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, supported in degree <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>. Our computation shows that the summand <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sgn_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>sgn</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sgn_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is naturally identified with <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(J^{\star}_{0,2})\otimes H(G^{(3,1)})[-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(J^{\star}_{0,2})\otimes H(G^{(3,1)})[-1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we turn to the second summand in Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm7" title="Theorem 1.7. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.7</span></a>.
The first nontrivial class is found in <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gr_{2}H_{c}^{12}({\mathcal{M}}_{4,3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>gr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>12</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gr_{2}H_{c}^{12}({\mathcal{M}}_{4,3})</annotation></semantics></math>. It corresponds to the generator of <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}_{3}\otimes H^{6}(G^{(3,n)})[-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}_{3}\otimes H^{6}(G^{(3,n)})[-1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and is represented by the following degree 12 cocycle in <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X^{\star}_{4,3},\tilde{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X^{\star}_{4,3},\tilde{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
