<div id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, as explained in Remark <a href="#S8.Thmthm8" title="Remark 8.8. ‣ 8.4. The cohomology of 
          
            
              
              
                
                J
                ⋆
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  1
                  ,
                  n ‣ 8. Direct summands with marked points ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.8</span></a>, there is one more summand of <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gr_{2}H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>gr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gr_{2}H^{\bullet}_{c}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math> coming from <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> which is not mentioned in Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm7" title="Theorem 1.7. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Weight two compactly supported cohomology of moduli spaces of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.7</span></a>. The first case where this summand is nontrivial arises when <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g,n)=(4,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g,n)=(4,4)</annotation></semantics></math>. We then have <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{4}\cong\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>≅</mo><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{4}\cong\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the graph cocycle in <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X^{\star}_{4,4},\tilde{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X^{\star}_{4,4},\tilde{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to <math id="S8.SS4.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{4}\otimes H^{6}(G^{(3,1)})[-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{4}\otimes H^{6}(G^{(3,1)})[-1]</annotation></semantics></math> has the form</p>
