<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Next, if exactly one <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-decoration is adjacent to an internal vertex <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="A1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> as above and set <math id="A1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\gamma)=\frac{1}{2}\Gamma_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\gamma)=\frac{1}{2}\Gamma_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
